 .PP
+The \fBASN1_item_d2i_bio()\fR and \fBASN1_item_d2i_fp()\fR functions, including their
+\&\fB_ex\fR variants, also return NULL at a clean end of input. In that case the
+error queue is left unchanged, so a caller reading concatenated structures in
+a loop can distinguish a clean end of input from a decoding error by
+inspecting the error queue, for example with \fBERR_peek_error\fR\|(3).
